                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for jianyu &amp;lt;yujian@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/59555f83-1147-43aa-a105-9e7b5630aa3b" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/59555f83-1147-43aa-a105-9e7b5630aa3b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_73e failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;CMD: onyx-42vm6 /usr/sbin/lctl list_nids
Try to mount to MGS NID fd33:3981:3213:f010:0:5254:1b:cfa4@tcp50
mount.lustre: mount fd33:3981:3213:f010:0:5254:1b:cfa4@tcp50:/lustre at /mnt/lustre failed: Invalid argument
This may have multiple causes.
Is 'lustre' the correct filesystem name?
Are the mount options correct?
Check the syslog for more info.
 conf-sanity test_73e: @@@@@@ FAIL: Mount fails on fd33:3981:3213:f010:0:5254:1b:cfa4@tcp50 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

